    "text": "I am a software engineer with 7 years of experience, and I am looking for a new job. Can you create a resume for me and explain each section?\n\n---\n\n**Resume: Software Engineer**\n\n**[Your Name]**  \n[Your Address] | [City, State, ZIP Code] | [Phone Number] | [Email Address] | [LinkedIn Profile (if applicable)] | [GitHub Profile (if applicable)]\n\n---\n\n### **Highlighted Section: Professional Summary**  \nA brief, concise statement that highlights your key skills, experience, and career goals. It should be tailored to the job you're applying for and showcase your strengths in a few sentences.\n\n---\n\n### **Highlighted Section: Education**  \nProvides your educational background, including the institution, degree, major, and year of graduation. It also includes relevant coursework or projects that are relevant to the job you're applying for.\n\n---\n\n### **Highlighted Section: Professional Experience**  \nThis is the most important section of the resume. It lists your work experience, including the company name, job title, dates of employment, and key responsibilities and achievements. It should be organized in reverse chronological order.\n\n---\n\n### **Highlighted Section: Technical Skills**  \nA list of your technical skills, including programming languages, frameworks, databases, operating systems, and other relevant tools. This section helps employers quickly understand your technical capabilities.\n\n---\n\n### **Highlighted Section: Certifications & Languages**  \nIf applicable, list any certifications you have (e.g., AWS Certified Solutions Architect, Google Cloud Certification) and your proficiency in languages (e.g., \"Fluent in English, Intermediate in Spanish\"). This section adds value if you have language skills or certifications that are relevant to the job.",
